# CODEOWNERS — who must review what.
#
# `main` is protected: every pull request needs an approving review from
# the owner of the paths it touches. The catch-all below means that is
# true for all changes. The explicit entries under it are not redundant —
# they document WHICH paths carry research or capital consequences, so a
# contributor can see the risk before opening the PR rather than after.
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md for what each group means in practice.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: everything needs owner review.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                       @martex-dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE LEDGER — the project's only real asset.
#
# A change here can invalidate every published verdict without breaking
# a single test. Pre-registration rules apply (CONTRIBUTING.md §2):
# a hypothesis doc is committed BEFORE its test runs, and every evaluated
# candidate counts as a trial — including cells nobody read.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
/PROJECT_MEMORY.md                      @martex-dev
/PROJECT_STATE.md                       @martex-dev
/CLAUDE.md                              @martex-dev
/docs/hypotheses/                       @martex-dev
/docs/research/ledger/                  @martex-dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# REPRODUCIBILITY GATES — these define what "unchanged" means.
#
# baseline.py declares the fingerprint inputs; the golden tests enforce
# them. Editing either can silence a regression rather than fix it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/martex_quant/research/baseline.py  @martex-dev
/tests/test_research_golden.py          @martex-dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# CAPITAL PATH — risk limits, kill switch, broker adapters, live config.
#
# The risk layer has veto power over every order and nothing may bypass
# it. Going live is a deliberate CLI step, never a dashboard button, and
# the guard's KILLED latch is cleared only by a human.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/martex_quant/risk_management/      @martex-dev
/src/martex_quant/live/                 @martex-dev
/src/martex_quant/execution/            @martex-dev
/docs/research/eval-runbook.md          @martex-dev
/docs/research/eval-runbook-sprint-amendment.md @martex-dev
/config/                                @martex-dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROJECT PLUMBING — CI, release, and these rules themselves.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                               @martex-dev
/pyproject.toml                         @martex-dev
/CONTRIBUTING.md                        @martex-dev
